1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,860
A denied claim should not leave an entry-level biller guessing.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:08,016
Claim Coach brings denial-management guidance into Hermes Desktop, with private, local models

3
00:00:08,016 --> 00:00:11,380
and a clear path from evidence to a reviewable draft.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,655
Start in Hermes Desktop. Open Capabilities, choose Plugins, rescan, and enable Claim

5
00:00:16,655 --> 00:00:20,710
Coach. Open the Claim Coach pane. This is where you create cases

6
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:22,400
and work through each denial.

7
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,773
Configure Hermes to use a model server on this Mac. The model

8
00:00:26,773 --> 00:00:28,360
weights live in your Models folder.

9
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:32,380
Claim Coach has its own local worker, which routes document processing and

10
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,680
drafting to local models.

11
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:39,202
Create a case and add the denial letter, an explanation of benefits,

12
00:00:39,202 --> 00:00:43,503
or pasted eight thirty-five text. Our example uses fictional data from Northstar

13
00:00:43,503 --> 00:00:44,220
Demo Health.

14
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:46,500
Process the case to read its fields.

15
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,347
Review the payer, service dates, amounts, and denial codes. Confirm any fields

16
00:00:52,347 --> 00:00:56,220
the software could not read. The example denial concerns authorization.

17
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:00,220
Keep the original evidence beside the structured fields while checking them.

18
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:05,513
Run diagnosis to get a plain-language explanation and a checklist of missing

19
00:01:05,513 --> 00:01:08,233
documents. Review the rule card and appeal deadline.

20
00:01:08,353 --> 00:01:11,585
These are decision aids: the biller checks the evidence and decides what

21
00:01:11,585 --> 00:01:12,393
to do next.

22
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:17,700
Request an appeal draft, or a corrected-claim checklist when that is the

23
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:21,800
right remedy. Edit and save the result, then export it for review.

24
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,960
Claim Coach does not send appeals or submit claims.

25
00:01:26,167 --> 00:01:30,487
In Hermes chat, use the denial command with a case identifier. The

26
00:01:30,487 --> 00:01:32,287
denial-triage skill guides the agent.

27
00:01:32,407 --> 00:01:36,807
Its tools retrieve code explanations, payer rules, and a redacted case summary,

28
00:01:36,807 --> 00:01:39,007
without handing over the source documents.

29
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:44,896
The Hermes loop reads your request, chooses a tool, inspects the result,

30
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:48,393
and continues. Skills supply the playbook. Commands provide shortcuts.

31
00:01:48,513 --> 00:01:52,575
Local models do the inference, while the plugin keeps the case workflow

32
00:01:52,575 --> 00:01:52,913
organized.

33
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,333
Record the final outcome when it is known. Claim Coach turns specialist

34
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:01,133
workflow into practical guidance on a consumer laptop.

35
00:02:01,253 --> 00:02:05,470
Private evidence, useful next steps, and a person in control of every

36
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:06,173
final decision.
